    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full `mvn test` build passes green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` rule for `POST /api/owners` with low structural impact \u2014 a new cohesive function class carries the logic, and the classes I edited stayed simple.\n\n**Behaviour**: On owner creation, `customerCode` is assigned as `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` \u2014 LAST3 is the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`, NNNN is a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count (e.g. `SMI-0007`). It runs before the save step, so the not-yet-persisted owner is excluded from the count, giving a strictly increasing global sequence.\n\n**Changes**:\n- **New** `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` function class (`.../rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 the entire rule, isolated with zero surrounding complexity.\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted an `assignCustomerCode` step between `ensureUniqueTelephone` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added the `customer_code` field plus a plain getter/setter (two trivial methods).\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema; MapStruct auto-maps it into `OwnerDto`, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it with no mapper change.\n- SQL: added the `customer_code` column to all four `schema.sql` variants (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) and appended a `NULL` to the positional seed `INSERT`s in `hsqldb`/`mysql` `data.sql` (h2/postgres seeds use explicit column lists, so they needed no data change).\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreFormatAndGlobalSequence`) and the full suite pass green.",
